From: Amperstrand <141745238+Amperstrand@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 22:44:42 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Re-enable endpoints on STM32F469 after OUT transactions

The STM32F469's USB OTG core reports core_id 0x0000_1200 and needs the
same F446-class workaround as the 0x0000_2000/0x0000_2100 cores:
after an OUT transaction completes, the endpoint must be re-enabled or
the core accepts no further OUT transfers.

Without this, a STM32F469I-DISCO device answers EP0 and then goes
silent after the first OUT transaction, so no interface endpoint ever
delivers data to the host.

Add 0x0000_1200 to the existing core_id condition (3 lines). Verified
on an STM32F469I-DISCO bench build; tracked downstream as
Amperstrand/ccid-firmware-rs#271.
---
 src/bus.rs | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/bus.rs b/src/bus.rs
index c36bad7..6942e6b 100644
--- a/src/bus.rs
+++ b/src/bus.rs
@@ -737,8 +737,9 @@ impl<USB: UsbPeripheral> usb_device::bus::UsbBus for UsbBus<USB> {
                                     .fill_from_fifo(*regs, data_size as u16, is_setup)
                                     .ok();
 
-                                // Re-enable the endpoint, F446-like chips only
-                                if core_id == 0x0000_2000
+                                // Re-enable the endpoint, F446-like chips and STM32F469
+                                if core_id == 0x0000_1200  // STM32F469 needs re-enablement
+                                    || core_id == 0x0000_2000
                                     || core_id == 0x0000_2100
                                     || core_id == 0x0000_2300
                                     || core_id == 0x0000_3000
